header=f'''# RenalRounds v0.10.0 · 30 October 2026

Search is the first visible control. Large titles, introductory paragraphs and coverage blocks have been removed from above it. A compact text-size / manual day-night / eGFR toolbar follows search. Filters start collapsed. Renal dosing leads each drug entry; PK and secondary copy/print/coverage tools follow it. Sources, coverage and offline-update details are below the findings. A small fixed ↶ button returns through in-app medicine/setting/search history; each dialog also has a back arrow that closes the panel. It never leaves the app. Calculator inputs are excluded from navigation history and still clear on close.

Day/night preference is saved independently of the system theme, with light as the first-use default. Text-size controls retain 100%, 115%, 130% and 150%. Enlarged tables stack on narrow phones. Favourites, theme and text size use browser-local preferences when storage is available; patient calculator inputs are not persisted.

This release adds 40 selected adult renal profiles and 3 product-information PK panels. The inventory remains 668 entries: {c['renal']} partial renal profiles, {c['safety']} shared safety notes and {c['catalog']} catalog entries without renal guidance. There are {p['profiles']} PK profiles; {p['allFourCoreFields']} contain all four core items, including qualitative IHD product statements where expressly qualified. These are not all measured modern circuit-clearance studies.

New additions include cardiovascular/diuretic/lipid drugs, 11 BPH/bladder agents, 6 allergy/respiratory agents and 8 GI/constipation agents. Some entries provide caution or insufficient-data guidance without numeric doses. Selected product labels/SmPCs were checked on 30 October; existing sources retain their original dates. BNF monograph reconciliation and independent clinical approval remain pending. All older drug regimens and PK panels are retained unchanged.

Key distinctions: perindopril erbumine versus arginine strengths and unassigned exact cutoffs; fenofibrate product-specific starting doses and dialysis contraindication; mirabegron indexed MDRD measure; indexed CLcr wording for solifenacin/tamsulosin; IR versus ER trospium/tolterodine/oxybutynin; tiotropium capsules for inhalation only; aluminium toxicity risk with sucralfate. No CKD table is copied into missing RRT modalities.

This remains incomplete: REMAINING_MEDICATIONS.json lists {len(remaining)} entries without drug-specific renal profiles ({c['catalog']} catalog entries plus {c['safety']} shared safety notes). Existing renal profiles also retain indication, formulation and RRT gaps. No entry has independent clinical approval.

'''
(D/'CHANGELOG.md').write_text(header+'## Earlier releases · historical\n\n'+(R/'changelog_v09.md').read_text())
(D/'EDITORIAL_GUIDE.md').write_text(header+'## Existing editorial policy · historical release record\n\n'+(R/'editorial_guide_v09.md').read_text())
(D/'SOURCE_AUDIT.md').write_text(header+'## v0.10 selected source IDs\n\n'+'\n'.join('- '+sources['v10-'+i]['id']+': '+sources['v10-'+i]['url'] for i in changed)+'\n\n## Prior source audit\n\n'+(R/'source_audit_v09.md').read_text())
(D/'COMPLETION_PLAN.md').write_text(header+'''## Remaining clinical work

Use the remaining-medications export and the full completion queue to prioritise the local adult formulary. Complete each indication/formulation and prescription-specific IHD, systemic PD, CRRT and PIRRT/SLED regimen. Reconcile source disagreements and kidney-function measures. Verify the local authorised product and obtain independent nephrology and renal-pharmacy sign-off before clinical release. The search inventory does not establish medicine availability or prescribing suitability.
''')
(D/'VERIFICATION.md').write_text('''# v0.10 verification

Run checks.mjs, checks_v10.mjs, checks_interface.mjs and checks_calculator.mjs after the full ordered build. They verify schema/source provenance, unchanged v0.9 records and prior PK/regimens, selected high-consequence thresholds/formulations/units, remaining-work exports, actual search functions, in-app navigation history, manual theme persistence/fallback, text control logic, calculator arithmetic and privacy, embedded documents/data, and actual service-worker offline/update/cache-isolation contracts.

Browser checks cover search-first order, collapsed filters, day/night toggling and reload persistence, back navigation through drugs/settings and dialog closure, enlarged clinical fonts, narrow phone overflow and the retained calculator. Fresh extraction/build and byte comparison verify package reproducibility; ZIP CRC and root SHA256 sums are checked.

Software and arithmetic checks do not establish clinical validity. BNF reconciliation, complete clinical coverage and independent approval remain pending. A physical phone and hosted HTTPS offline installation/update require verification after GitHub upload.
''')
